## Requirements needed for this simulation to run

# Functional Requirements

The simulator ideally should:

- Model a 52-lap race around Silverstone
- Model Soft, Medium and Hard tyre compounds
- Calculate fuel mass loss and defecit for each lap
- Calculate tyre degradation as tyre age increases
- Calculate an estimated lap time for each lap
- Simulate complete tyre stints
- Simulate one-stop race strategies
- Simulate two-stop race strategies (if possible)
- Include pit-stop time losses
- Compare different race strategies
- Identify the strategy with the minimum simulated race time

# Modelling Requirements

The mathematical model should:

- Account for the effect of fuel mass on lap time
- Reduce fuel mass as the race progresses
- Account for tyre compound performance
- Account for tyre degradation with tyre age
- Model tyre degradation as a nonlinear effect
- Reset tyre age when a new tyre is fitted
- Add a time penalty when a pit stop occurs

# Optimisation Requirements

- Evaluate multiple tyre compound combinations
- Evaluate multiple possible pit-stop laps
- Exclude invalid strategies
- Identify the strategy with the minimum race time
- Compare one-stop and two-stop strategies

# Required outputs

- Total race time
- Tyre compounds used
- Pit-stop lap or laps
- Lap-by-lap race data
- Fuel mass for each lap
- Tyre age for each lap
- Calculated lap time for each lap
- Strategy comparison results
- Graphical results for tyre degradation and strategy performance

# Validation Requirements

These things need to be checked: (hard limits/ things that just don't make any sense)

- Fuel mass never becomes negative
- Fuel mass decreases through the race
- Tyre degradation increases with tyre age
- Fresh tyres begin with a tyre age of zero
- Total race time equals the sum of lap times and pit-stop losses
- Invalid tyre compounds are rejected
- Invalid pit-stop laps are rejected
- The optimiser returns the fastest strategy from those evaluated

# Project Constraints

The initial model:

- Focus on Silverstone only
- Use simplified tyre degradation parameters
- Use simplified fuel-consumption assumptions
- Avoid proprietary Formula 1 telemetry
- Run on a standard laptop
- Be developed within approximately two weeks

# Initial Scope Exclusions

The first version will not include:

- Weather complications
- Safety Car or Virtual Safety Car scenarios
- Traffic (blue flags or lap one racing)
- Overtaking
- Tyre temperature
- Detailed vehicle dynamics
- ERS deployment
- Component failures
